  "name": "Wobble Shot",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "The lineage wobble: Square Morph with a one-shot Mod A (1/8, Decay) kicking the Index on every hit, light Saturate, then a resonant Filter A LP12 whose cutoff Mod B wobbles with a sine synced to 1/8T (locked to the host grid), over a clean sine sub at the played pitch. Play: 1/8 riddim patterns around F1-A#1 with the transport running; the triplet wobble runs against the straight notes, so every hit lands on a different part of the wobble. Tweak: Mod B Division for the wobble rate, Mod B Cutoff for depth, Filter A Freq and Res for the squelch, Mod A Index amount for the hit. Macro plan (not wired yet): Wobble = Mod B Cutoff amount, Tone = Filter A Freq, Squelch = Filter A Res, Hit = Mod A Index amount. FX: Overdrive +8 dB with a Post low-pass at 8 kHz so the wobble's top edge bites, multiband squash at 80 % with fast time, an EQ low cut at 25 Hz and -3 dB at 500 Hz, Dimension (size 0.5, wet low cut 150 Hz) and a 6 % short plate.",
